ADDITIONAL NOTICE (not a modification of the MIT terms above)

gask is an unofficial tool. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported
by Google LLC. "Google" and "AI Mode" are trademarks of Google LLC.

gask automates a web browser to send questions to Google AI Mode. Google does not
offer a public API for AI Mode, and automated querying may violate Google's Terms
of Service. By using gask you accept that:

  1. You alone are responsible for complying with Google's Terms of Service and
     any other terms, laws or policies that apply to your use.

  2. Google may detect automated or high-volume use and may, without notice,
     show captchas, rate-limit, or temporarily or permanently block the IP
     address, network, browser profile or Google account the queries come from.
     A block can also affect normal Google searching and other Google services
     for everyone sharing that IP address (for example, a home or office
     network).

  3. The built-in safeguards (one query at a time, a minimum gap between
     queries, captcha detection) reduce this risk but do not prevent it. Use
     gask lightly and for personal research.

  4. Answers are generated by an AI model and may be wrong, incomplete or out
     of date. Verify them against the cited sources before relying on them.
     Do not send secrets or personal data in questions; every question is
     sent to Google.

The authors are not liable for any block, suspension, loss of access, or other
consequence of using gask, as stated in the warranty disclaimer above.
